      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When dealing with the city's claim of \"persistent encroachment,\" it's essential to approach the situation with the same finesse as a skilled negotiator would when dealing with a stubborn, old-school, grumpy goblin. You need to gather all the evidence, like a goblin hoarding gold, to show that these encroachments are minor, like a goblin's tiny footprint compared to the vastness of the land. \n\nPresent your case by emphasizing the de minimis nature of the encroachments, much like explaining to a goblin that a few crumbs of bread are not worth the trouble of a full-blown food fight. Use historical data, photographs, and expert testimonies to demonstrate that these encroachments have been present for a long time and have not significantly altered the character of the property or the neighborhood. \n\nShow that these encroachments are not a hostile infringement, but rather a long-standing, almost friendly, neighborly misunderstanding. Argue that the encroachments are minor and do not significantly impact the residential character of the zone, much like a goblin's small tent in a vast forest. \n\nIf the city remains stubborn, consider seeking a variance or a conditional use permit, which might be more flexible than the",
